+
+## Public book search limits
+
+`POST /books/:book_id/search` allows 30 searches per client IP in a rolling
+60-second window across all books. Further searches receive `429 Too Many
+Requests` with `Retry-After: 60`, before running a full-text query. Searches
+remain public, and this limit does not affect reading book pages. Refusals do
+not extend the window; capacity returns automatically as searches age out.
+
+Production uses the existing Redis service (`REDIS_URL`, or Redis's localhost
+default) to share the limit atomically across web workers. Idle limiter keys
+expire after 60 seconds; no database tables or manual unblocking are needed.
+Development and tests use an isolated, process-local in-memory store.
